From 4e2d819a2d31e5f12b6b84c5f4fab1fb3c2c1452 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Medium1992 <Medium1992@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:44:29 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] XHTTP client: Hedge a hanging dial only with
 XRAY_XHTTP_DIAL_HEDGE=on

While a handshake hangs, a hedged dial sends up to three more ClientHellos
to the server within seconds, the kind of connection burst Jolymmiles/
Xray-core guards against (TestHTTP2ClientSharesOneDialWhileHandshakeHangs,
taken here): a censor may block on it. Hedging is now off unless
XRAY_XHTTP_DIAL_HEDGE is on, true or 1; off, a dial waits on its one
attempt until the 10s handshake bound, as in v26.11.9-h2Flow-2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
